For actual text, text_removals may accept/correct initial hyphen/whitespace joins using exact anchors from the ORIGINAL layout.text; omit or [] preserves the original. Never remove letters, numbers or reference markers. These literal whitespace/hyphen edits may cross formatting nodes or OCR formula wrappers; this does not authorize rewriting words or mathematical content. This is a source-local edit declaration, not permission for free rewriting. Sources /title, /caption and /content expose intrinsic DISPLAY fields with original asset geometry. They may be split, reassigned or restored to body/notes like other text sources. Preserve structured table nodes; never flatten them. Final accepted text/heading decisions will not be re-guessed downstream.
